-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/e13b3025-d1a9-55eb-b5e0-22786eced9d6
-- title:
--   Uniqueness of the closed point on an Igusa component over s
-- statement:
--   The setting is that of the Igusa/Drinfeld chart data for a full-level modular curve, descended to a henselian base.
--
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, and let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)(M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ (this field being the intermediate field generated by the two Laurent expansions $j$ and $j(q^{M'}\cdot)$ over the residue field) such that, by `hW`, a place belongs to $W$ exactly when it is supersingular in the sense of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: it is rational, it is an affine geometric place, and its value at the generator $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ lies in the supersingular $j$-set $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$. Let `hle` assert the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field into the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` for $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)(M')$, i.e. a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places compatible with degrees and with order functions, and the compatibility with $A$ and its residue map recorded in the structure; `hR₀` requires in addition that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Let $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfy $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$, and let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an element of $\mathrm{Idx}\,q$).
--
--   The two families of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ are $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, indexed by the lines $\ell \in \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q) = \mathrm{CuspidalType.ProjLine}\,q$, and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$, indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, which describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ as the set of $f$ expressible as a quotient $x/y$ of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose denominator has nonzero coefficientwise reduction, in the form $f \cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; `hIg`, which provides for each $\ell$ some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma \cdot \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q = \ell$ and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ equal to the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, which for every root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ gives a permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q)$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ pulled back along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ equal to $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\sigma\ell)$ for all $\ell$.
--
--   The supersingular hypotheses are four. `hSS_A`: for each $s$ and each $x \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the image of $x$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ if and only if $x \in A$. `hSS_over`: for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which $\hat\jmath$ — the element $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,\mathrm{jq}$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ — has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ under the inclusion given by `hle` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and moreover for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference between the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal. `hSS_fix`: each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is stable under pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr`: for each $s \in W$ there is $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t$ minus the image of any $a \in A$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   The descent data are as follows. $K_0$ is a subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ algebraic over it and $\pi \in K_0$; $A_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation domain; $\iota : A_0 \to A$ is an injective local ring homomorphism whose composite range in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is exactly $A \cap K_0$ (`hιK₀`), such that the residue map of $A$ composed with $\iota$ is surjective (`hres`); $\varpi_0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_0$ (`hϖ₀`) and its image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is $\pi$ (`hϖ₀π`). $F_0$ is a subfield of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ characterised by `hF₀` as the set of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$; by `hjF₀` the image of $\hat\jmath$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $F_0$, and this element of $F_0$ is nonzero. $F_0$ carries an $A_0$-algebra structure whose structure map agrees, after inclusion into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, with $\iota$ followed by the inclusion of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hj₀`).
--
--   Write $C = \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,F_0\,\hat\jmath$, the $A_0$-subalgebra of $F_0$ of elements integral over $A_0[\hat\jmath]$. Fix $s \in W$, a line $\ell \in \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q)$, and two maximal ideals $\mathfrak n, \mathfrak n'$ of $C$ subject to two pairs of conditions. The component conditions `hℓ`, `hℓ'` state that every $g \in C$ whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is a nonunit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ lies in $\mathfrak n$, respectively in $\mathfrak n'$. The floor-trace conditions `htr`, `htr'` state that for every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which is regular wherever $\hat\jmath$ is (in the sense of the order condition above) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, for every $a \in A_0$ with $\mathrm{residue}\,A\,(\iota a)$ equal to $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, every $g \in C$ whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ equals the image of $f$ minus the image of $\iota a$ lies in $\mathfrak n$, respectively in $\mathfrak n'$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the single equality $\mathfrak n = \mathfrak n'$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the statement that a fixed Igusa component of the descended two-chart integral model carries exactly one closed point above a given supersingular place of the floor: any two maximal ideals of the finite chart algebra which contain the nonunits coming from $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and have floor trace $s$ coincide. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isMaximal_mem_iff_mem_maximalIdeal_drinfeldRing_unique_chartAlgFin_descent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isMaximal_mem_iff_mem_maximalIdeal_drinfeldRing_unique_chartAlgFin_descent), which combines it with the corresponding existence statement.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_eq_of_isMaximal_of_mem_nonunits_igusaRing_of_floorTrace_chartAlgFin_descent.lean

